hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1339","Hilal bin Bishr told us, Abdul Wahhab bin Abdul Majeed told us, Khaled told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Minhal, on the authority of Abu Barza: that the Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace, he “hated sleeping before dinner, and did not like to talk after it.” Abu Bakr said in Shaqiq’s report, on the authority of Abdullah, He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, brought sunburnt to us after dark.”"
"1340","Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Habib bin Al-Shahid told us, Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, Yusuf bin Musa told us, Jarir told us, both of them on the authority of Ata Ibn Al-Sa'ib, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: I heard Muhammad Ibn Muammar saying: Abdul-Samad said: “By slander he means slander.”"
